{"body":"## Summary\nValidate feedback and remediation thresholds before rubric scoring reads or writes state. Non-finite or out-of-range thresholds now raise InvalidRubricScoringError, and remediation cannot exceed feedback. Valid inclusive bounds and equal thresholds preserve existing correctness and feedback behavior.\n\nCloses #673\n\n## Tasks\n- [x] Enforce finite unit-interval bounds and relative threshold ordering in score_attempt_with_rubric.\n- [x] Cover invalid values, rejection without durable scoring side effects, continued session use, and valid threshold boundaries.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `python -m pytest tests/feedback/test_rubric_scoring.py -q --no-cov` — 42 passed.\n- [x] NaN feedback threshold raises the exact documented InvalidRubricScoringError with HTTP status 422.\n- [x] Feedback 0.4 and remediation 0.8 raises `remediation_threshold cannot exceed feedback_threshold`.\n- [x] Deliberate break tested and reverted: removing all three guards made the 13 invalid-input cases fail; restoring guards returned the suite to green.\n\n## Validation\n`python -m pytest tests/feedback -q --no-cov` — 134 passed. Focused mypy (two files), Ruff, Black, and git diff --check passed. Rejection tests commit without rollback and verify evidence, rubric-score, feedback, action, queue, and card row counts remain unchanged before successfully scoring the same attempt. Valid zero/one and equal thresholds cover correctness, review, and remediation boundaries.\n\n<!-- deliberate-break: test=tests/feedback/test_rubric_scoring.py::test_rubric_scoring_rejects_invalid_thresholds_without_writes test-file=tests/feedback/test_rubric_scoring.py break-file=src/lms/feedback/scoring.py -->\n\nLocal validation evidence: opener run 20260919T220136Z, acceptance-tests.txt, deliberate-break.txt, feedback-restored.txt, and mypy.txt. CI and the elapsed post-push review remain with keepalive/closer.\n\n<!-- pr-preamble:start -->\n<!-- meta:issue:673 -->\n> **Source:** Issue #673\n\nCloses #673\n\n<!-- pr-preamble:end -->\n\n<!-- auto-status-summary:start -->\n## Automated Status Summary\n#### Scope\nIn `score_attempt_with_rubric` (`src/lms/feedback/scoring.py:77-165`), `feedback_threshold: float = 0.85` and `remediation_threshold: float = 0.5` are consumed in boolean checks (`normalized_score >= feedback_threshold`, `normalized_score < feedback_threshold`, `normalized_score < remediation_threshold`) without validating that they are finite numbers in `[0.0, 1.0]` and that `remediation_threshold <= feedback_threshold`. Passing `float('nan')` causes `normalized_score >= nan` and `normalized_score < nan` to both evaluate to `False`, falsely marking a 100% attempt as failed (`correctness=False`) while simultaneously suppressing feedback creation.\n\n#### Tasks\n1. [ ] In `src/lms/feedback/scoring.py`, validate in `score_attempt_with_rubric` that `math.isfinite(feedback_threshold)` and `0.0 <= feedback_threshold <= 1.0` (raising `InvalidRubricScoringError(\"feedback_threshold must be a finite number between 0.0 and 1.0\")`).\n2. [ ] Validate that `math.isfinite(remediation_threshold)` and `0.0 <= remediation_threshold <= 1.0` (raising `InvalidRubricScoringError(\"remediation_threshold must be a finite number between 0.0 and 1.0\")`).\n3. [ ] Validate that `remediation_threshold <= feedback_threshold` (raising `InvalidRubricScoringError(\"remediation_threshold cannot exceed feedback_threshold\")`).\n4. [ ] In `tests/feedback/test_rubric_scoring.py`, add test cases asserting `InvalidRubricScoringError` when non-finite, out-of-range, or inverted thresholds are supplied to `score_attempt_with_rubric`.\n\n#### Acceptance criteria\n- [x] Running `pytest tests/feedback/test_rubric_scoring.py` passes cleanly.\n- [x] Calling `score_attempt_with_rubric(session, ..., feedback_threshold=float('nan'))` raises `InvalidRubricScoringError(\"feedback_threshold must be a finite number between 0.0 and 1.0\")`.\n- [x] Calling `score_attempt_with_rubric(session, ..., feedback_threshold=0.4, remediation_threshold=0.8)` raises `InvalidRubricScoringError(\"remediation_threshold cannot exceed feedback_threshold\")`.\n- [x] Deliberately breaking the validation logic causes the targeted tests to fail.\n\n<!-- auto-status-summary:end -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **Bug Fixes**\n  - Rubric scoring now rejects invalid, non-finite, or out-of-range feedback and remediation thresholds.\n  - Configurations with a remediation threshold above the feedback threshold are rejected.\n  - Invalid threshold configurations return clear validation errors before database changes occur.\n  - Boundary values and resulting feedback and correctness levels are handled consistently.\n  - Failed validation no longer disrupts subsequent scoring operations or leave unintended persistence effects.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","closingIssuesReferences":[{"id":"I_kwDOSm8tI88AAAABQte8Nw","number":673,"repository":{"id":"R_kgDOSm8tIw","name":"learning-management-system","owner":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDQ2MzIy","login":"stranske"}},"url":"https://github.com/stranske/learning-management-system/issues/673"}],"labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDOSm8tI88AAAACkkwsEw","name":"agent:codex","description":"Assign to Codex agent","color":"0e8a16"},{"id":"LA_kwDOSm8tI88AAAACkkwsIQ","name":"agents:keepalive","description":"Enable keepalive monitoring on PR","color":"1d76db"},{"id":"LA_kwDOSm8tI88AAAACkkwsNg","name":"autofix","description":"Let bots format/lint automatically","color":"0366d6"},{"id":"LA_kwDOSm8tI88AAAACkk75eg","name":"verify:compare","description":"Runs verifier comparison mode after merge","color":"942665"},{"id":"LA_kwDOSm8tI88AAAAC0VgzwQ","name":"codex","description":"Created by Codex","color":"6f42c1"}],"mergeCommit":{"oid":"4e9d3f10acd5597438f9e3b691281921b6ecbde8"},"mergedAt":"2026-09-20T01:25:43Z","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","compl